Description: find Qt6 GuiPrivate package explicitly for Qt >= 6.10
 KF6WindowSystem, the X11 plugin and the KWayland plugin all link
 Qt6::GuiPrivate (the wayland one via the versionless Qt::GuiPrivate
 alias). Since Qt 6.10 the private module targets are split into
 standalone CMake packages and are no longer created by the main
 module's find_package call, so CMake generation fails against
 Qt 6.12 with:
 .
   Target "KF6WindowSystem" links to:
   Qt6::GuiPrivate
   but the target was not found.
 .
 Add a version-gated find_package(Qt6 REQUIRED COMPONENTS GuiPrivate)
 right after the top-level find_package(Qt6Gui) call, making the
 private target (and its versionless alias) visible to every
 subdirectory. Builds against Qt <= 6.9 are unchanged.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-16

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -42,6 +42,12 @@
 # Dependencies
 set(REQUIRED_QT_VERSION 6.5.0)
 find_package(Qt6Gui ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED)
+# Qt 6.10 起，私有模块目标(如 Qt6::GuiPrivate)拆分为独立的 CMake 包，
+# 不再随主模块的 find_package 自动创建，需要显式查找，否则 CMake 配置阶段报
+# "Target ... links to: Qt6::GuiPrivate but the target was not found"。
+if(Qt6Gui_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL 6.10)
+    find_package(Qt6 REQUIRED COMPONENTS GuiPrivate)
+endif()
 
 option(KWINDOWSYSTEM_QML "Build QML bindings" ON)
 
